2. Stage 0 Is Broadly Consistent Across Operators

Stage 0 is relatively similar across the individual metric-only runs.

Typical observations:

• Stage 0 duration: approximately 8–12 minutes
• Stage 0 shuffle write: approximately 1.15–1.17 TiB
• Stage 0 median task duration: around 0.2 seconds
• Stage 0 execution memory: approximately 64 MiB median

This consistency is important.

The large runtime differences between operators are not primarily being created in Stage 0.

The major divergence appears after the first shuffle boundary, in Stage 1 and, for five operators, Stage 2.

This supports the conclusion that the operator-specific cost is being introduced by the downstream metric-processing path.

