8. fv4_metric_8 Is the Key Exception

Configuration size

fv4_metric_8 contains 25 metrics.

Observed execution

• Approximate runtime: ~40 minutes
• Stage 0: approximately 11 minutes
• Stage 1: 29 minutes
• No heavy Stage 2
• Stage 1 shuffle read: 1,144.3 GiB
• Stage 1 memory spill: 4.4 GiB
• Stage 1 disk spill: 94.7 MiB
• Stage 1 median task: 1.2 minutes
• Stage 1 maximum task: 14 minutes
• Stage 1 median shuffle read: 58.4 MiB
• Stage 1 maximum shuffle read: 195.1 MiB

Interpretation

fv4_metric_8 is fundamentally different from the other five operators.

It completes after the first downstream stage and does not exhibit the same second-stage shuffle/spill pattern.

Compared with the expensive operators, spill falls from roughly:

• 124–152 GiB memory spill to 4.4 GiB
• 7–10 GiB disk spill to only 94.7 MiB

The maximum task duration also falls to 14 minutes.

This makes fv4_metric_8 the most important comparison operator for Engineering / Data Science.

