9. Recurring Stage 2 Pattern Across Five Operators

The following operators all produce an expensive second downstream stage:

• gen_metric_1
• gen_metric_2
• gen_metric_3
• fv2_metric_6
• frdrt_metric_7

Across these operators, Stage 2 consistently shows:

• final shuffle read of approximately 1.2–1.37 TiB
• memory spill of approximately 124–152 GiB
• disk spill of approximately 7–10 GiB
• maximum tasks of approximately 33–45 minutes
• median shuffle partitions around 60–70 MiB
• maximum shuffle partitions around 2.7–3.3 GiB

This is a recurring execution signature rather than an isolated anomaly.

Long-tail / partition imbalance

Typical final-stage task:

• around 45–60 seconds
• around 60–70 MiB shuffle read

Extreme task:

• around 33–45 minutes
• around 2.7–3.3 GiB shuffle read

This demonstrates that a small number of tasks are receiving substantially more data than the typical task.

The likely technical area to inspect is therefore the partition distribution created by metric Group By / window / aggregation logic.

