Conclusion

The individual metric-only benchmarks show that the Metrics layer is not computationally uniform.

gen_metric_1 is currently the most expensive tested operator, but the broader finding is more important:

> **Five operators independently reproduce the same expensive second-stage shuffle/spill pattern, while `fv4_metric_8` does not.**

This indicates that the key optimisation opportunity is not simply reducing the absolute number of metrics.

The stronger optimisation approach is to:

1. identify the expensive metric structures,
2. identify which of those metrics are genuinely required,
3. remove or redesign high-cost / low-value calculations,
4. validate the resulting lean metric population in the complete Model Plan.

The upstream Map operators are deliberately excluded from these benchmarks and must be considered separately when evaluating full end-to-end Model Plan runtime.